.TH CLOG_GET_LEVEL 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
clog_get_level \- return the current minimum log level
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/clogger.h>

clog_level_t clog_get_level(clog logger);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the minimum severity level that the logger has at the moment of
the call.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
logger  Logger handle.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The current minimum level.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Thread-safe.  Each logger keeps its minimum level in an atomic value of
its own, apart from the lock that serialises the writes and the rotation
of the shared output target, so reading the level of one logger never
contends with a write that a sibling logger on the same target has in
progress.
Asserts when logger is CLOG_INVALID, stale or already closed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clog_set_level (3)
